+## Reverse proxy authentication
+
+To sign users in through a trusted reverse proxy, set these options in `navidrome.toml`:
+
+```toml
+ReverseProxyWhitelist = "192.0.2.0/24,2001:db8::/32"
+ReverseProxyUserHeader = "Remote-User"
+```
+
+`ReverseProxyWhitelist` is empty by default, which disables this feature. It accepts IPv4 and IPv6 CIDR ranges, individual IP addresses, and `@` for a Unix socket. The header defaults to `Remote-User`. Users are created on their first proxy login; the first user becomes an administrator.
+
+Configure the proxy to remove any client-supplied `Remote-User` header and set it only after authenticating the request. Limit the whitelist to the proxy's connection addresses; a broad range such as `0.0.0.0/0` lets other clients supply the username header.
+
